    {
      "text": "Give to him that asketh thee, Matt. 5:42 (Luke 6:30; 3 Ne. 12:42). Ask, and it shall be given you, Matt. 7:7 (D&C 4:7). promised … to give her whatsoever she would ask, Matt. 14:7 (Mark 6:22). asked his disciples … Whom do men say that I … am, Matt. 16:13 (Mark 8:27; Luke 9:18). Ye know not what ye ask, Matt. 20:22 (Mark 10:38). committed much, of him they will ask the more, Luke 12:48. thou, being a Jew, askest drink of me, John 4:9. none of the disciples durst ask him, John 21:12. asking no question for conscience sake, 1 Cor. 10:25. let them ask their husbands at home, 1 Cor. 14:35. able to do exceeding abundantly above all that we ask, Eph. 3:20. If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, James 1:5 (JS—H 1:11).",
